> **rakkarage:** i can just make a placeholder dynamic font and set size to 1

In v4.0.alpha.calinou [e363f404a], I tried leaving the default font and just setting the font size (Control:Theme Overrides/Font Sizes/Font Size).

* Setting to 1 seemed to have no effect on the minimum size.
* Setting to 2 DID reduce the minimum size.
* Setting to 1, after having set it to 2, started working as expected, reducing the minimum size further than 2 did.

Given the inconsistent results, I'd recommend 2 for folks looking for a workaround to get shorter buttons... if they don't mind a couple pixels of unavoidable minimum height. I didn't need a placeholder font.
.
.
Also surprisingly, when expand_icon is true, hseparation (space between text and icon) is included in the draw calculation.

[Excerpt](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/a743bcef4dfaf97c128a245121709f5f23de7a25/scene/gui/button.cpp#L257-L259): button.cpp, _notification(NOTIFICATION_DRAW)
````
if (!_icon.is_null()) {
	// ...
	if (expand_icon) {
		Size2 _size = get_size() - style->get_offset() * 2;
		_size.width -= get_theme_constant(SNAME("hseparation")) + icon_ofs_region;
		// ...
		if (icon_width > _size.width) {
			icon_width = _size.width;
			icon_height = _icon->get_height() * icon_width / _icon->get_width();
		}
````

Setting "Expand Icon" on a button already at minimum size scales down the icon, when I would've expected it to remain unscaled at that size.

The scaling occurs because the default hseparation=2 eats away at the icon's width. It effectively creates a single pixel gap on the left and right of the icon. A gap between the icon and the stylebox's border.

Again, I would not have expected hseparation to apply when text is "".

It's even conditional already: when NO icon is set, hseparation is ignored. Left & right stylebox borders can squeeze together to touch.

As a workaround, I'd recommend setting Control:Theme Overrides/Constants/Hseparation=0.
.
.
**tl;dr:** Using both workarounds (the small font size and zeroed hseparation), folks can make icon-only buttons whose content meets the border, vertically & horizontally at the icon's native size.
